-- title:
--   Generator of mathfrak m_{C,x} has order one at the place of x
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $L$ a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, and let $M$ be a curve model of $L/K$ in the sense of the project's structure `CurveModel`: a scheme $C$ over $K$ (via a morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} K$) that is integral, proper over $K$ and smooth of relative dimension $1$, together with a ring isomorphism `ffEquiv` from $L$ onto the function field of $C$ compatible with the map of $K$ into the function field induced by the structure morphism, a bijection `placeOfPoint` from the closed points of $C$ onto the places of $L/K$ (a place being a valuation subring of $L$ containing the image of $K$, different from $L$ itself, and a principal ideal ring) such that for each closed point $x$ the image of the stalk $\mathcal O_{C,x}$ in $L$ under `ffEquiv.symm` composed with the canonical map to the function field is exactly the valuation subring of the place attached to $x$, and the property that every finite set of points of $C$ lies in an affine open. Let $x$ be a closed point of $C$ and let $g$ be an element of the stalk $\mathcal O_{C,x}$ whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Then the element of $L$ obtained from $g$ by the canonical map of $\mathcal O_{C,x}$ into the function field followed by `ffEquiv.symm` has `ord` equal to $1$ at the place `placeOfPoint x`, where `ord` denotes minus the `WithZero` logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the place.
--
--   This is the statement that a generator of the maximal ideal of the local ring at a closed point of a smooth proper curve model is a local uniformiser for the corresponding place, so that its order there is exactly one. It is used to convert statements produced by étale charts and local coordinates (e.g. on models of modular curves) into order computations at places, and is cited in particular by the existence result for functions of order one at a point and by the chart-based order computations on the models `XHDRModelAtP`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel_ord_placeOfPoint_ffEquiv_symm_algebraMap_eq_one_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing

universe u v

theorem AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.ord_placeOfPoint_ffEquiv_symm_algebraMap_eq_one_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span
    {K : Type u} [Field K] {L : Type v} [Field L] [Algebra K L]
    (M : AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel K L) (x : closedPoints M.C) (g : M.C.presheaf.stalk x.1)
    (hg : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (M.C.presheaf.stalk x.1) = Ideal.span {g}) :
    (M.placeOfPoint x).ord (M.ffEquiv.symm (algebraMap (M.C.presheaf.stalk x.1) M.C.functionField g)) = 1 := by sorry
